abstract: >-
  A new exact value of a book Ramsey number, R(B_57, B_58) = 231, the case n = 58 of Wesley's
  conjecture R(B_{n-1}, B_n) = 4n - 1 and its smallest open case before this work: a graph on 230
  vertices, a two-block circulant graph over Z_115 of the shape Turturean uses for even n, with no
  B_57 whose complement has no B_58. The proof reduces both book conditions to 57 inequalities. The
  repository also gives a hand-checkable proof of R(B_66, B_67) = 267, first shown by Chung, Du and
  Wesley in the Station data of 24 August 2026, by a graph over Z_133 whose connection sets are unions
  of orbits of the cube roots of unity. It holds both papers, Lean 4 proofs of both values (the
  graphs checked by the kernel, the upper bound by Goodman's count; standard axioms only),
  independent checks in C and Python, the searches, and dated priority checks.
